Minato's patch to frameworks/base's core/java/android/net/VpnService.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0), group 1 of
the framework breadth (vpn-test): Builder.verifyApp without the IPackageManager stub.

Why: addAllowedApplication and addDisallowedApplication check the package with
IPackageManager.Stub.asInterface(ServiceManager.getService("package")).getApplicationInfo, a call into a
compile-only stub, which ART cannot resolve (NoClassDefFoundError in the app; tools/framework-check.sh's stub
references). The app's own package manager, which ApplicationPackageManager answers over the app's manifest, does
the same work. IPackageManager answers null for a package that is not installed and the Builder takes no notice of
it: the AVD's Android 15 accepts addAllowedApplication and addDisallowedApplication of a package that is not
installed without an exception [verified: vpn-test, "builder allowed missing: ok"], so ApplicationPackageManager's
NameNotFoundException is swallowed.

tools/build-framework.sh applies it to a copy in build/framework/src, never to build/sources.

--- a/core/java/android/net/VpnService.java
+++ b/core/java/android/net/VpnService.java
@@ -779,13 +779,13 @@
         }
 
         private void verifyApp(String packageName) throws PackageManager.NameNotFoundException {
-            IPackageManager pm = IPackageManager.Stub.asInterface(
-                    ServiceManager.getService("package"));
-            try {
-                pm.getApplicationInfo(packageName, 0, UserHandle.getCallingUserId());
-            } catch (RemoteException e) {
-                throw new IllegalStateException(e);
-            }
+            // Minato asks the app's own package manager, not the IPackageManager stub. IPackageManager answers
+            // null for a package that is not installed and the Builder ignores it: so does this.
+            try {
+                VpnService.this.getPackageManager().getApplicationInfo(packageName, 0);
+            } catch (PackageManager.NameNotFoundException e) {
+                // not installed: Android's Builder accepts it all the same
+            }
         }
 
